<title>USA: Airlease ups stake in leased aircraft.</title>
<headline>Airlease ups stake in leased aircraft.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airlease Ltd said it bought a 50 percent stake in the MD-82 aircraft currently leased to Trans World Airlines Inc, bringing its ownership interest to 100 percent.</p>
<p>The aircraft had been jointly held with USL Capital Corp the previous parent of the general partner of Airlease Ltd.</p>
<p>As a result of having sole ownership, the partnership obtained new financing of $9 million, which exceeds the purchase price of the 50 percent interest in the aircraft, it said.</p>
<p>The balance of the funds will be used for working capital purposes.</p>
</text>
